// endpoint_adjust_feed_text_scale.proto — AdjustFeedTextScale: nudge the feed
// text zoom one small step up or down. FEED section.
//
// The user zooms the FEED TEXT (and only the feed text) with `C-+` / `C--` in
// Emacs, held down for continuous fine adjustment. Each press sends ONE nudge;
// the DAEMON owns the scale — it applies a fixed small step, clamps it to a
// sane range, and PERSISTS it so the zoom survives a daemon restart. The
// resulting scale is PUSHED to every open feed's watch (frontend.v1.FeedTextScale)
// so the webapp re-scales its feed text, and is ACKED here so the caller can
// echo it.
//
// The scale is a SINGLE DAEMON-GLOBAL preference applied to every feed, not a
// per-workspace one: "the feed text size" is one setting, and the simplest
// match for that is one value. The request therefore carries NO WorkspaceRef —
// there is no per-workspace ownership to refuse on, which is why the response
// has no error arms (unlike SetModel / SelectResponse). The client sends only a
// DIRECTION; the daemon is the source of truth for the step and the clamp,
// exactly as it is for the response-selection cursor.

